#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204089 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203852 :question/id #uuid "fd07ad0f-548a-5569-84de-d658a88c4b9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-17087" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$\n\n- $2z - 5 = z + 1$\n\n- $3z - 2 = 3z - 2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+3 & =4z+9 \\\\ 4z+3-4z & =4z+9-4z \\\\ 3 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-5 & =z+1 \\\\ 2z-5-z+5 & =z+1-z+5 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2z - 5 = z + 1$ has the unique solution $z = 6.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z-2 & =3z-2 \\\\ 3z-2-3z & =3z-2-3z \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048213 :topic/math-academy-id 343 :topic/title "Solving Linear Equations With Variables on Both Sides"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957f5ab3-d388-5802-b6c6-5558fc72d19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203505} {:answer/id #uuid "073992da-065c-598a-8f0c-75308325aff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203506} {:answer/id #uuid "266a49b8-bc53-50c0-822f-5b3fdc58778c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203507} {:answer/id #uuid "289f48b6-c744-5b4c-ac43-bb7c3b60ead4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203508} {:answer/id #uuid "46217fe4-5804-5c9e-ae53-96c797906451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203509}] :answer-field/id #uuid "110de02f-a175-5ac8-8341-249e977c4adf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203504}] :question/id #uuid "d5d365bc-e325-5d06-ae8b-3799791feb02" :question/math-academy-id "q-287964" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n1. $2x = x + 1$\n2. $2x + 1 = 2x + 1$\n3. $2x + 1 = 2x + 3$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85183c94-e141-50ef-945b-894dbe2fe6be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203511} {:answer/id #uuid "99928875-8585-539b-a856-da07dd6fd1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203512} {:answer/id #uuid "df332339-0c54-528c-9ada-ee89985519d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203513} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2d8ffc-a69d-5fdb-b341-6e99f1e6830b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203514} {:answer/id #uuid "75aac1bc-0989-5fdf-a037-6f51b15ba95e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203515}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0b4d3b-494b-55d4-9523-196ee64019a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203510}] :question/id #uuid "6bda3cab-2f65-5bfd-a054-8baee9c84dc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-288058" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n1. $4x - 2 = 4x + 3$\n2. $3x + 4 = 3x + 4$\n3. $5x = 2x + 6$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c8ed87-cb43-5db0-be5c-e831e6121bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295822} {:answer/id #uuid "70fd28f2-8ceb-5fae-b21c-0d8c37373df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295886} {:answer/id #uuid "992814b5-63ad-57d1-9bda-8a6d0aea5b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296088} {:answer/id #uuid "efc85614-0678-5ede-96c5-eeebb1586b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296543} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc665d1-d05c-5d6a-bc20-c9ca8c023c4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efc85614-0678-5ede-96c5-eeebb1586b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296543} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a661465-5e98-54ef-82ac-034599d77271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296959}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b892079-10a1-5d68-a34f-01695fac566e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288066" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $-3u+4=-3u-1$\n- $2u+5=2u+8$\n- $6u-2=3u+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+4 & =-3u-1 \\\\ -3u+4+3u & =-3u-1+3u \\\\ 4 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $-3u+4=-3u-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+5 & =2u+8 \\\\ 2u+5-2u & =2u+8-2u \\\\ 5 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u+5=2u+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =3u+1 \\\\ 6u-2-3u+2 & =3u+1-3u+2 \\\\ 3u & =3 \\\\ u & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $6u-2=3u+1$ has the unique solution $u=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e935809-7eff-5524-8f2e-8f4f21f5d685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295440} {:answer/id #uuid "276266b0-8b3d-5094-8f78-2c2d0df618f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295484} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc10199-d63c-5736-b2b0-1c0ef77650f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295796} {:answer/id #uuid "e00d1820-af62-5599-b6e8-6dccf62f726a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296455} {:answer/id #uuid "ff69cb28-f522-54a1-8193-c2a2130eae30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276266b0-8b3d-5094-8f78-2c2d0df618f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295484} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f3788ac-8209-560a-917f-1cc30dcfba9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296927}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e1fdbd8-4927-548c-aafb-62f0ed007aa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288070" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $-4y+2=-4y-5$\n- $6y+3=6y-1$\n- $5y-7=2y+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+2 & =-4y-5 \\\\ -4y+2+4y & =-4y-5+4y \\\\ 2 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-4y+2=-4y-5$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+3 & =6y-1 \\\\ 6y+3-6y & =6y-1-6y \\\\ 3 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $6y+3=6y-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-7 & =2y+1 \\\\ 5y-7-2y+7 & =2y+1-2y+7 \\\\ 3y & =8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $5y-7=2y+1$ has the unique solution $y=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29f682ce-814d-576c-9d68-46eaffd55e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295506} {:answer/id #uuid "34d91129-90ea-5ce1-ba6a-b94c177abdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295562} {:answer/id #uuid "5d99b17d-1345-5edc-934a-f0e572fd837c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295806} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b35403-5d7a-5721-b22e-eb61699d25cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296474} {:answer/id #uuid "f194dee2-3414-5e50-8807-b8317095ddfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d99b17d-1345-5edc-934a-f0e572fd837c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295806} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c9470b-a03d-5e8c-a6cc-e7fb12154e33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296645}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22403a37-d9b4-5866-bee2-a28d9c27c3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-288072" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $2z-4=2z+1$\n- $5z+6=5z+6$\n- $3z+2=z+4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-4 & =2z+1 \\\\ 2z-4-2z & =2z+1-2z \\\\ -4 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $2z-4=2z+1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z+6 & =5z+6 \\\\ 5z+6-5z & =5z+6-5z \\\\ 6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+2 & =z+4 \\\\ 3z+2-z-2 & =z+4-z-2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3z+2=z+4$ has the unique solution $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ec15b0-9006-57c3-a6ed-6a7ffae1f559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295450} {:answer/id #uuid "483443d7-d949-50ec-a7b8-e99c24e9079f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295680} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0712b9-1553-53a1-83a6-c73d8f9df552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296012} {:answer/id #uuid "8f108ee3-0807-5637-839d-91c354641014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296029} {:answer/id #uuid "9d46e37c-b28f-5c45-9927-cdb6e5e1fe53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f108ee3-0807-5637-839d-91c354641014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296029} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8696e8-0827-512c-9081-1eb13fb3de19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae9bca83-e68f-5756-9519-1447b4343c01" :question/math-academy-id "q-288073" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $3w+2=2w+2$\n- $4w-7=4w-7$\n- $6w+5=6w+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w+2 & =2w+2 \\\\ 3w+2-2w-2 & =2w+2-2w-2 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3w+2=2w+2$ has the unique solution $w=0.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w-7 & =4w-7 \\\\ 4w-7-4w & =4w-7-4w \\\\ -7 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w+5 & =6w+9 \\\\ 6w+5-6w & =6w+9-6w \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $6w+5=6w+9$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d604b35-b182-51ef-8ad8-153a353f0418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295529} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2e8c0b-8871-52a8-8f7e-27c536e84a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295618} {:answer/id #uuid "560da999-55c4-5b56-a1d6-481d32f3a37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295765} {:answer/id #uuid "a943da63-fb2b-5fdc-9bc3-6074acd881a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296157} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c83eab-72fe-5dac-9261-1a12e8b33cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d604b35-b182-51ef-8ad8-153a353f0418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295529} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a845396-80e0-59b7-bded-5ac38a7616cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296777}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6480ee2c-c900-5448-85b3-32f94538971e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288074" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $9v-5=4v+2$\n- $2v+3=2v+7$\n- $5v-1=5v-1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-5 & =4v+2 \\\\ 9v-5-4v+5 & =4v+2-4v+5 \\\\ 5v & =7 \\\\ v & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $9v-5=4v+2$ has the unique solution $v=\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+3 & =2v+7 \\\\ 2v+3-2v & =2v+7-2v \\\\ 3 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $2v+3=2v+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-1 & =5v-1 \\\\ 5v-1-5v & =5v-1-5v \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204090 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203853 :question/id #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" :question/math-academy-id "e-17213" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4(r - 2)y = -8\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(r-2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4(r-2)}{4} & =\\frac{0}{4} \\\\ r-2 & =0 \\\\ r & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203491} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b1d5cd-7280-5a3b-b538-d976044c6e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203492} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfa0123-90e9-5186-b54d-3ae7859972b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203493} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb6287c-2e23-513c-b813-c514eaaaaae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203494} {:answer/id #uuid "7dffe079-6e58-5eee-a2d4-f50f9c6c606c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203495}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b9422b9e-c65d-596a-90ac-20fde363b97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203490}] :question/id #uuid "b6c453dd-3b6b-5f65-bf37-1fc261d1f26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-287665" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2px = 3$\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab2ed61-9a09-5b11-8a3a-164d58ee2841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295425} {:answer/id #uuid "3661811c-5e94-5d73-b96b-461bf4e8e913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295572} {:answer/id #uuid "40b4c162-fdcc-5a2f-b9e5-cbff3a9f1ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295638} {:answer/id #uuid "47a2b01c-7509-53de-83a6-61b8b988976f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295675} {:answer/id #uuid "9875c009-5dc6-5f7c-aa43-8e5947cacf7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47a2b01c-7509-53de-83a6-61b8b988976f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295675} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a0300a-10ae-558b-8e38-4e29591d58b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "328a41df-8074-5d3e-9600-d58da9a2fa99" :question/math-academy-id "q-288593" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q-1)y=4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=q-1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-1 & =0 \\\\ q & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a358628-bbab-5730-aa92-30852d8b8b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295319} {:answer/id #uuid "13781b68-e9a2-5ebc-b3a8-d9a9f51cced6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295375} {:answer/id #uuid "28fc5cf6-6471-5d82-bb36-92f61e00662f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295498} {:answer/id #uuid "38232641-7f92-55ce-8842-067f6f7fcb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295582} {:answer/id #uuid "a107bd3a-590a-5785-8899-90e2f9d4863d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a358628-bbab-5730-aa92-30852d8b8b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295319} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26af55d-71ac-5eea-97e8-97cf35cab8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297009}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5cf9073-af1e-5711-af30-8567dad9e870" :question/math-academy-id "q-288135" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4py=-2\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=4p,\\,b=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4p=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9cd574-87f6-5684-a4a2-52f23dcc4f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295323} {:answer/id #uuid "4512c30d-0418-5d1a-a9a4-5767ffaddbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295659} {:answer/id #uuid "4e445b8e-50d5-51d4-9056-86f12aba889d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295718} {:answer/id #uuid "967246bb-eb10-50c8-9141-55173f83e32f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296068} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ae615f-ae70-595f-a21b-63e9d4cc1379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2ae615f-ae70-595f-a21b-63e9d4cc1379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296210} :answer-field/id #uuid "078b8df7-1fda-503a-8213-ba030a04d1b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d84e977-5f76-5e6a-86a0-a01877993e64" :question/math-academy-id "q-288143" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3(q+4)x=6\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=-3(q+4),\\,b=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3(q+4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(q+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-3(q+4)}{-3} & =\\frac{0}{-3} \\\\ q+4 & =0 \\\\ q & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0eba8c-0b29-5b5a-b4c3-fc5fa03d4285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295356} {:answer/id #uuid "13856c1d-